<?xml version="1.0" encoding="windows-1252"?>
<!--
  Sample business questions for the Northwind Business Analyst Agent example
  (northwind-analyst). Each <question> becomes one prompt sent to
  PromptRunner:generateText() with NorthwindQueryTool attached; the LLM
  calls ExecuteQuery() one or more times to retrieve the data it needs.

  Data spans 2024 - June 2026. 2025 is used as the reference full year;
  question 2 compares 2024 vs 2025; question 5 compares H1 2025 vs H1 2026.

  The <internal> element is metadata for the reader (which SQL pattern each
  scenario is meant to exercise) - the loader ignores it and only reads
  <text>.
-->
<questions>

  <!-- 1 -->
  <question>
    <internal>Top 5 products by 2025 revenue with percentage share. Exercises: CTE + multi-table JOIN + aggregation + percentage of total.</internal>
    <text>Which are the top 5 products by total revenue in 2025? Show product name, category name, total revenue rounded to 2 decimal places, and each product's percentage share of the total 2025 revenue.</text>
  </question>

  <!-- 2 -->
  <question>
    <internal>Quarterly revenue comparison 2024 vs 2025 with YoY growth. Exercises: date grouping + conditional aggregation + YoY growth %.</internal>
    <text>Compare quarterly sales revenue for 2024 and 2025 side by side. For each quarter (Q1 through Q4), show total revenue for both years and the year-over-year growth percentage rounded to 1 decimal place.</text>
  </question>

  <!-- 3 -->
  <question>
    <internal>High-frequency customers below average spend in 2025. Exercises: HAVING filter + subquery for average comparison.</internal>
    <text>Which customers placed more than 5 orders in 2025 but had a total spend below the average customer spend that year? Show company name, country, order count, and total spend rounded to 2 decimal places, sorted by total spend descending.</text>
  </question>

  <!-- 4 -->
  <question>
    <internal>Top 3 employees by 2025 revenue with best product category. Exercises: multi-level aggregation + per-employee top-category lookup.</internal>
    <text>Who were the top 3 sales employees by total revenue in 2025? For each employee show full name, total revenue rounded to 2 decimal places, number of orders handled, and the name of their highest-revenue product category.</text>
  </question>

  <!-- 5 -->
  <question>
    <internal>Categories with YoY H1 revenue decline (H1 2025 vs H1 2026). Exercises: YoY H1 conditional aggregation + decline filter + sort.</internal>
    <text>Which product categories had lower revenue in the first half of 2026 (January through June 2026) compared to the same period in 2025? Show category name, H1 2025 revenue, H1 2026 revenue (both rounded to 2 decimal places), and the decline percentage rounded to 1 decimal place, sorted by largest decline first.</text>
  </question>

</questions>
